VirtualBox VM Setup
1. Download & Preparation

    Download Fedora Server 42 ISO from getfedora.org
    
    Open VirtualBox and create new virtual machine

2. VM Configuration

    Type: Linux
    
    Version: Fedora (64-bit)
    
    RAM: Minimum 2 GB (4 GB recommended for XFCE)
    
    Storage: 20 GB virtual hard disk (dynamic allocation)
    
    CPU: 2+ cores for better performance

3. Storage & Network

    Settings → Storage: Attach Fedora ISO to virtual optical drive
    
    Network: Ensure adapter is enabled (NAT or Bridged)

Fedora Server Installation
1. Boot & Install

    Start VM - boots into Fedora installer
    
    Select "Install Fedora Server 42" from boot menu

2. Anaconda Installer Steps

    Choose language and keyboard layout
    
    Configure storage (automatic partitioning recommended)
    
    Set root password
    
    Create user account
    
    Begin installation

3. Post-Installation

    Reboot VM after installation completes
    
    Important: Remove ISO from storage settings
    
    System boots from virtual hard disk

System Setup & GUI Installation
1. System Update

    sudo dnf upgrade -y - Update all packages to latest versions
    
    -y flag automatically confirms prompts

2. Install XFCE Desktop

    sudo dnf install @xfce-desktop-environment - Install XFCE desktop group
    
    Note: @ symbol indicates package group/environment installation
    
    Includes X.org display server and all XFCE components

3. Set Graphical Default

    sudo systemctl set-default graphical.target - Set GUI as default boot target
    
    Changes from text-only to graphical interface

4. Final Reboot

    sudo reboot - Restart system
    
    System loads into graphical login manager (LightDM/GDM)
    
    Login with user credentials to access XFCE desktop

Verification
    Successful boot into XFCE desktop environment
    
    Responsive graphical interface while maintaining server capabilities

    Full Fedora Server functionality in virtualized environment
